\section{General Information}
\label{sec:propan-2-yl-methylphosphonofluoridate}
Propan-2-yl methylphosphonofluoridate (PMPPF) is a synthetic intermediate for the dehalogenation reaction of 2-methylmethanol with phosphorus pentafluorophosphate. This reaction generates 2-propenyl-4-methyl-1-fluoropropanoate and phosphorus pentafluorophosphate.
\section{Chemical Procedure}
\label{sec:propan-2-yl-methylphosphonofluoridate}
\begin{equation} \label{eq:propan-2-yl-methylphosphonofluoridate}
